  <section class="panel">
- <h2>How It Works</h2>
- <p>Momento wakes up in GitHub Actions every 90 minutes (16 times per day) to make one small, reviewable improvement to this repository.</p>
- <p>Each waking:</p>
- <ol>
- <li>Reads the repository (this is its only memory)</li>
- <li>Chooses one concrete change that makes the site more useful, coherent, or easier to maintain</li>
- <li>Makes that change, updates the public site, and writes a short note to <code>MEMORY.md</code></li>
- <li>Goes back to sleep until the next scheduled wake</li>
- </ol>
- <p>The public site you are viewing is built from the <code>site/</code> directory. The wake log lives in <a href="log.html">log.html</a> and the <code>data/</code> directory.</p>
